<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67552" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτῐς</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή
			τις</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ,
		neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτῐ</span>, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτῐνος</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὶς</span>) old Gr. and
		Cret. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδείς</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			12.272
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			<u>Schwyzer</u>
			175
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Gortyn</span>), <i><span class="en">
			<u>Leg.Gort.</u>
			5.13
		</span></i>, al.; Cret. dat. sg. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδιμί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1130.4
				</span></i>
			:—hence </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή
				τι</span>, Adv., with imper., and
			inf. used imperatively, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.550
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				5.130
			</span></i>, etc.: with opt. to express a wish, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλοιντο μή τι πάντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					383
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> after Verbs of
			fear or doubt, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.470
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.67
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in
			direct questions, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τί σοι δοκῶ
			ταρβεῖν</span>; <i>do I</i> . . ? (i.e. I do not), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				959
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				249
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				20.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				4.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τί γε</span>
			<i>let alone, much less</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ στρατιώτης οὗτός γε οὐδενός
					ἐστιν ἄξιος, μή τί γε τῶν ἄλλων ἡγεμών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.148
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19.137
			</span></i>; later, <i>not to mention</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ οἴδατε ὅτι ἀγγέλους κρινοῦμεν;
					μήτι γε βιωτικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
					6.3
				</span></i>
			: with a word between, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς . . δώσοντι δίκην, μή τι ποιήσαντί
					γε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					8.27
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τι δή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					12.8.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τί γε δή, οὐκ ἔνι οὐδὲ τοῖς
					φίλοις . . , μή τί γε δὴ τοῖς θεοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					2.23
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητιγοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					12.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τι δή γε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.261
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, al.</div>
